---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/docs.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Packages — Querial">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-querial-indigo-on-dark">For Developers</p>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mt-1">Packages</h1>
            <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground max-w-3xl">
                A package is a portable, code-based tree of one or more pipelines.
                Codes are identity. Secrets never travel in the tree. Git is optional.
                Import always lands as drafts in the current project.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 [&>p]:text-muted-foreground [&>h2]:text-foreground [&>h3]:text-foreground">
            <h2>What a package is</h2>
            <p>
                The canonical form is a UTF-8 directory tree. A zip is only a transport
                of that tree. A Git working copy <em>is</em> that tree — never zip-as-source-of-truth.
                The root manifest must declare <code class="text-foreground">format: querial.package/v1</code>.
                Unknown major versions are rejected. Additive fields (retry, join mode,
                schema sources, <code class="text-foreground">external-parquet</code>)
                did not bump the format.
            </p>
            <p>
                This role authors the tree. Operators import, remap connections, and
                (when allowed) create stubs. Publish remains Querial’s immutable version
                gate: import never writes a published version.
            </p>

            <h2>Canonical tree</h2>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>querial.package.yaml
connections/catalog.yaml
schema-sources/catalog.yaml   # optional; stubs only
pipelines/
  &lt;pipeline.code&gt;/
    pipeline.yaml
    README.md                 # optional operator guide
    sql/steps/*.sql           # path as declared in pipeline.yaml
    sql/migrations/*.sql</code></pre>
            <p>
                SQL file paths are whatever <code class="text-foreground">pipeline.yaml</code>
                declares (forward slashes). Labs often use
                <code class="text-foreground">sql/steps/</code> and
                <code class="text-foreground">sql/migrations/</code>. An optional
                <code class="text-foreground">schemas/</code> folder is reserved for
                vendored JSON Schemas for editors — it is <em>not</em> the schema-source
                catalog. Do not put <code class="text-foreground">schema-sources/catalog.yaml</code>
                under <code class="text-foreground">schemas/</code>.
            </p>
            <p>
                Optional <code class="text-foreground">x-export</code> on
                <code class="text-foreground">pipeline.yaml</code> is provenance.
                Import must ignore it for publish authority.
            </p>

            <h2>Root manifest</h2>
            <p>
                Required: <code class="text-foreground">format</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">code</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">pipelines[]</code> (at least one).
                Package <code class="text-foreground">code</code> is a slug:
                <code class="text-foreground">^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]*$</code>. Pipeline
                codes use underscores, not hyphens:
                <code class="text-foreground">^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_]*$</code>.
            </p>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>format: querial.package/v1
code: aw-scenario-e
name: AdventureWorks Scenario E
description: Parquet spine with DuckDB transforms and dual staged sinks.
revision: duckdb-join-v1
pipelines:
  - code: aw_scenario_e
    path: pipelines/aw_scenario_e</code></pre>
            <p>
                <code class="text-foreground">revision</code> is informational (SemVer
                or a dated stamp). It is not Querial’s
                <code class="text-foreground">pipeline_versions.version_number</code>.
                <code class="text-foreground">path</code> is relative, forward slashes.
                One zip = one package root. A combined lab zip lists several pipelines
                in the same manifest (A through E).
            </p>

            <h2>Codes are identity</h2>
            <p>
                Import creates database GUIDs. Never put those GUIDs in the package.
                Identity in the tree:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li>Package: <code class="text-foreground">package.code</code></li>
                <li>Pipeline / step / migration / parameter: their <code class="text-foreground">code</code></li>
                <li>Edges: <code class="text-foreground">from</code> and <code class="text-foreground">to</code> step codes</li>
                <li>Logical connection: <code class="text-foreground">name</code> in <code class="text-foreground">connections/catalog.yaml</code></li>
                <li>Schema source: <code class="text-foreground">code</code> in <code class="text-foreground">schema-sources/catalog.yaml</code>, referenced as <code class="text-foreground">schema:</code> on a step or migration</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Connections catalog — stubs only</h2>
            <p>
                Never include connection strings, passwords, tokens, host/port/database
                users, or ciphertext.
            </p>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>connections:
  - name: aw-source
    provider: sqlserver
    description: AdventureWorks source logical connection stub.
  - name: aw-sql-dest
    provider: sqlserver
    description: SQL Server destination stub.
  - name: aw-pg-dest
    provider: postgresql
    description: PostgreSQL destination stub.</code></pre>
            <p>
                Allowed providers in v1: <code class="text-foreground">postgresql</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">sqlserver</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">mysql</code>.
            </p>
            <p>
                Each <code class="text-foreground">pipeline.yaml</code> may list
                allow-list names (including unused). Omitted lists are inferred from
                step and migration <code class="text-foreground">connection:</code>
                values. Import writes the pipeline–connection allow-list from that
                union <em>before</em> inserting bound steps.
            </p>
            <p>
                Unresolved stubs block materialization. Interactive import / Git
                activate opens a wizard: <strong class="text-foreground">use existing</strong>
                or <strong class="text-foreground">create</strong> (optionally with a
                Development endpoint). API/CLI may supply an explicit
                <strong class="text-foreground">remap</strong> map, or
                <code class="text-foreground">require_existing</code> /
                <code class="text-foreground">create_stubs</code>. Creating stubs is
                an operator/admin action. Developers may export and import with remap
                or require-existing; inventing unresolved endpoints is not this role.
            </p>

            <h2>Schema sources catalog — stubs only</h2>
            <p>
                Optional. Export writes it only when exported pipelines bind at least
                one schema source. Stubs carry identity and include/exclude policy —
                never fetch strings.
            </p>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>schema_sources:
  - code: aw_sales
    name: AdventureWorks sales
    provider: sqlserver
    include_mode: listed
    include_schemas:
      - Sales
    exclude_schemas: []</code></pre>
            <p>
                <code class="text-foreground">include_mode</code> is
                <code class="text-foreground">all_user</code> or
                <code class="text-foreground">listed</code>. Bind with
                <code class="text-foreground">schema: aw_sales</code> on a step or
                migration. <code class="text-foreground">artifact-sql</code> must not
                set <code class="text-foreground">schema:</code>. Import resolves
                sources like connections. <code class="text-foreground">create_stubs</code>
                cannot invent fetch secrets — missing sources block until an operator
                creates them in the project. See
                <a href="/docs/developer-sql-assist" class="text-link hover:underline">SQL Assist</a>.
            </p>

            <h2>pipeline.yaml</h2>
            <p>
                Required: <code class="text-foreground">code</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">name</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">steps</code>. Optional metadata:
                <code class="text-foreground">description</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">readme</code> (relative path; default
                <code class="text-foreground">README.md</code> when the file exists),
                <code class="text-foreground">connections</code> allow-list,
                <code class="text-foreground">parameters</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">migrations</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">dependencies</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">migration_dependencies</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">layouts</code>.
            </p>
            <h3>Pipeline-level policy</h3>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li><code class="text-foreground">dag_failure_policy</code>: <code class="text-foreground">fail_fast</code> (default) or <code class="text-foreground">continue_independent</code>. Deployments may override.</li>
                <li><code class="text-foreground">retry</code> map: omit means max attempts 1 (off). See <a href="/docs/developer-retry" class="text-link hover:underline">Step retry policies</a>.</li>
            </ul>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>retry:
  max_attempts: 3
  backoff_seconds: 5
  backoff_multiplier: 2
  on_abandoned: false

dag_failure_policy: fail_fast</code></pre>

            <h3>Parameters</h3>
            <p>
                Each parameter needs <code class="text-foreground">code</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">display_name</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">param_type</code>. Optional:
                <code class="text-foreground">description</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">default_value</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">is_required</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">display_order</code>. Types used at
                trigger: string, integer, decimal, boolean, datetime, date. Defaults
                are not secrets; secret overlay still redacts in plan JSON.
            </p>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>parameters:
  - code: batch_label
    display_name: Batch label
    param_type: string
    default_value: lab
    is_required: true
    display_order: 1</code></pre>

            <h3>Steps</h3>
            <p>
                Required: <code class="text-foreground">code</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">name</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">type</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">execution_order</code>.
                <code class="text-foreground">sql</code> is a relative path and is
                required except for <code class="text-foreground">external-parquet</code>.
            </p>
            <div class="overflow-x-auto not-prose">
                <table class="w-full text-sm">
                    <thead><tr class="border-b border-border text-left"><th class="py-2 pr-4">type</th><th class="py-2">Role</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody class="text-muted-foreground">
                        <tr class="border-b border-border/50"><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-foreground">sql_command, sql_query, stored_procedure, validation_query, database-sql</td><td class="py-2">Dialect SQL on the bound target.</td></tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-border/50"><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-foreground">database-query-to-parquet</td><td class="py-2">Extract query → Parquet. <code class="text-foreground">config.outputName</code>.</td></tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-border/50"><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-foreground">artifact-sql</td><td class="py-2">DuckDB over named inputs. No connection. No <code class="text-foreground">schema:</code>.</td></tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-border/50"><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-foreground">staged-database-sql</td><td class="py-2">Only database sink. Stages use <code class="text-foreground">from_step</code> + <code class="text-foreground">columns[]</code>.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-foreground">external-parquet</td><td class="py-2">Upload root. No SQL, no connection. See <a href="/docs/developer-external-parquet" class="text-link hover:underline">External Parquet ingest</a>.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <p>
                Optional per step: <code class="text-foreground">connection</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">schema</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">transaction_mode</code>
                (<code class="text-foreground">required</code> |
                <code class="text-foreground">suppressed</code>),
                <code class="text-foreground">failure_policy</code>
                (<code class="text-foreground">fail_pipeline</code> |
                <code class="text-foreground">continue</code>),
                <code class="text-foreground">join_mode</code>
                (<code class="text-foreground">all</code> |
                <code class="text-foreground">any</code>; omit = Wait all),
                <code class="text-foreground">retry</code> override,
                <code class="text-foreground">unsafe_for_auto_retry</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">command_timeout_seconds</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">config</code> (handler JSON, no secrets).
            </p>
            <p>
                Export writes <code class="text-foreground">join_mode</code> only when
                it is Wait any. Wait any is rejected on Artifact SQL, Staged Database
                SQL, <code class="text-foreground">from_step</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">artifact_available</code> inbound edges,
                and indegree below two —
                <a href="/docs/developer-join-mode" class="text-link hover:underline">Wait all and Wait any</a>.
            </p>

            <h3>Extract, transform, sink config</h3>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code># Extract
type: database-query-to-parquet
connection: aw-source
sql: sql/steps/010_extract_sales_order.sql
config:
  outputName: sales_order

# DuckDB transform (single or multi input)
type: artifact-sql
sql: sql/steps/045_transform_order_summary.sql
config:
  outputName: order_summary
  inputs:
    - from_step: transform_sales_order
    - from_step: transform_sales_line

# Sink — never bake artifactId / storeUri / checksum
type: staged-database-sql
connection: aw-pg-dest
sql: sql/steps/100_load_order_summary_postgres.sql
config:
  stages:
    - from_step: transform_order_summary
      columns:
        - source: sales_order_id
          name: sales_order_id
          type: int
          nullable: false
  transaction:
    mode: stage-and-execute</code></pre>
            <p>
                <code class="text-foreground">stages</code> and
                <code class="text-foreground">inputs</code> are <strong class="text-foreground">lists</strong>.
                Map-shaped YAML is rejected. Qualifiers in SQL are producer
                <code class="text-foreground">outputName</code> values. One inbound file
                may use <code class="text-foreground">{"{{ stage }}"}</code> /
                <code class="text-foreground">{"{{ input }}"}</code>; several files need
                <code class="text-foreground">{"{{ input.sales_order_transformed }}"}</code>.
                Canvas edges are the binding UI —
                <a href="/docs/developer-handler-contracts" class="text-link hover:underline">Step handler contracts</a>.
                Import materializes frozen <code class="text-foreground">name</code> from
                producer <code class="text-foreground">outputName</code>; package YAML
                does not list it.
            </p>

            <h3>Edges</h3>
            <p>
                In <code class="text-foreground">dependencies</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">to</code> <strong class="text-foreground">depends on</strong>
                <code class="text-foreground">from</code>. Same for
                <code class="text-foreground">migration_dependencies</code>.
            </p>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>dependencies:
  - from: extract_sales_order
    to: transform_sales_order
    requirement: artifact_available
  - from: load_sales_order_sqlserver
    to: load_sales_line_sqlserver
    requirement: required</code></pre>
            <p>
                Package vocabulary: <code class="text-foreground">required</code>
                (predecessor must succeed) or <code class="text-foreground">optional</code>
                (must complete). Import also accepts Querial’s stored values
                <code class="text-foreground">succeeded</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">completed</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">artifact_available</code>. Default is
                required.
            </p>

            <h3>Layouts</h3>
            <p>
                Designer coordinates. Optional <code class="text-foreground">group_name</code>
                and <code class="text-foreground">color</code>. Not execution-authoritative.
            </p>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>layouts:
  - step: ingest_ids
    x: 80
    y: 80
  - step: load_ids
    x: 360
    y: 80</code></pre>

            <h3>Migrations</h3>
            <p>
                Ordered, coded SQL files. Required:
                <code class="text-foreground">code</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">name</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">execution_order</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">sql</code>. Optional connection and
                schema source. After apply, the <strong class="text-foreground">target
                database</strong> records what ran — restoring a backup does not confuse
                Querial. Per-pipeline <code class="text-foreground">README.md</code>
                is UTF-8, max 512 KiB, imported into the pipeline README field.
            </p>

            <h2>Where import lands</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li>Always the <strong class="text-foreground">current project</strong>. There is no cross-project share in v1 — copy means export then import.</li>
                <li>Always <strong class="text-foreground">drafts</strong>. You still publish in Workspace.</li>
                <li>Does not copy ciphertext. Endpoints stay in the project’s connection store after remap or create.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Zip vs Git</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li><strong class="text-foreground">Directory tree</strong> — source of truth. Validate this.</li>
                <li><strong class="text-foreground">Zip</strong> — portable snapshot of one package root.</li>
                <li><strong class="text-foreground">Git package-root</strong> — the working directory <em>is</em> the package (<code class="text-foreground">querial.package.yaml</code> at the root).</li>
                <li><strong class="text-foreground">Git workspace</strong> — repo contains <code class="text-foreground">packages/&lt;package.code&gt;/…</code>. Sync/publish/activate resolve per package code; siblings are left alone. Empty trees publish into workspace layout.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Mixing root and <code class="text-foreground">packages/*</code> in the
                same repo is rejected. Core operation never requires a remote. Operators
                configure remotes, Sync, publish-to-Git, and activate —
                <a href="/docs/devops-git" class="text-link hover:underline">Git and package remotes</a>.
                Agents do not need Git. Publication must not become a secret dump.
            </p>
            <p>
                Operators own clone/fetch/commit paths. See
                <a href="/docs/devops-git" class="text-link hover:underline">Git and package remotes</a>.
            </p>

            <h2>Validate, pack, unpack</h2>
            <p>
                JSON Schemas ship with the product under
                <code class="text-foreground">schemas/querial-package/v1/</code>:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li><code class="text-foreground">querial.package.schema.json</code></li>
                <li><code class="text-foreground">querial.connections.catalog.schema.json</code></li>
                <li><code class="text-foreground">querial.pipeline.schema.json</code></li>
                <li><code class="text-foreground">querial.schema-sources.catalog.schema.json</code></li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Validation is YAML → JSON → JSON Schema, then semantic checks (SQL
                files exist, dependency codes resolve, ingest has no SQL/connection,
                unique <code class="text-foreground">outputName</code>, and so on).
                A Package CLI exposes <code class="text-foreground">validate</code>,
                <code class="text-foreground">pack</code>, and
                <code class="text-foreground">unpack</code>. Editor YAML extensions
                can associate those schema files with the matching filenames.
            </p>

            <h2>AdventureWorks and ingest labs</h2>
            <p>
                Ready-made trees, zips, canonical SQL, and the packing script live on
                the <a href="/labs" class="text-link hover:underline">Labs</a> pages.
                Scenario E is extract → DuckDB join/aggregate → dual staged sinks.
                Scenario F is <code class="text-foreground">external-parquet</code>
                → PostgreSQL staged load and is not schedulable. Import is an operator
                action; this role reviews the draft DAG and publishes. Binding lists:
                <a href="/docs/developer-handler-contracts" class="text-link hover:underline">Step handler contracts</a>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
